From: OneKVM Project <223006751+lowtech-guy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vi: use a literal snprintf format

name_list contains data, not format strings.  Passing it as the format is
both unsafe and rejected by toolchains built with -Werror=format-security.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 modules/vi/src/dump_register.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/vi/src/dump_register.c b/modules/vi/src/dump_register.c
index e29cd2d..703f29c 100644
--- a/modules/vi/src/dump_register.c
+++ b/modules/vi/src/dump_register.c
@@ -1679,7 +1679,7 @@ static int dump_hw_register(VI_PIPE ViPipe, FILE *fp)
 			// SET_REGISTER_COMMON(0x4, 0, shdw_sel); // reg_shdw_read_sel
 			SET_REGISTER_COMMON(0x8, 0, enable); // reg_dpc_enable
 
-			snprintf(name, sizeof(name), name_list[i]);
+			snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "%s", name_list[i]);
 			FPRINTF_TBL(data_dpc);
 
 			free(data_dpc);
-- 
2.50.1
